{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>You shall keep My statutes.</b> He mentions statutes regarding pastoral work, agriculture, clothing, intercourse, food, drink, and divination of the future — in all these their conduct of life was engaged. Now, the majority of what He prohibited are matters contrary to the intent of nature, which is ordered by the Almighty, may He be exalted, who arranges it. Yet regarding the designated bondmaid — although it is a statute in which she is lashed and he is not, and in which he brings a sacrifice for the intentional act, and these two features are not found in any other commandment in the Torah — nevertheless He gave some reason for the matter, in saying:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:59.605048326Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}